Strata in the babylon_5 overlay
===============================

Layout
------
* /usr/bin/strata          - wrapper pinning STRATA_PYTHON to the ebuild's
                             interpreter (override with STRATA_PYTHON=...)
* /usr/share/strata/       - the Terminal tree (strata.py, CLI, Control,
                             the API server and its web assets)
* /usr/bin/strata-{plan,gguf,dequant} - engine utilities (every USE setup)
* /usr/lib/strata/engine/<version>-linux-x86_64-<backend>/
                           - engine component folder (USE=cuda/hip):
                             the engine binary, BUILD.json and, with
                             USE=vision, the picture reader

Engine registration (USE=cuda or USE=hip)
-----------------------------------------
Strata resolves engines per user, so register the system-built component
once:

    strata components add-build /usr/lib/strata/engine/<folder>
    strata components engines

CUDA architectures: Portage's sandbox cannot see the GPU, so without an
override the engine is compiled for the fallback list 80;86;89;120 (no PTX)
with a warning. Pin exactly what you need via /etc/portage/package.env:

    app-ai/strata strata-arch.conf      # STRATA_CUDA_ARCHS="120"

nvcc (CUDA toolkit 12.8/12.9) rejects host compilers newer than gcc 14, so
the CUDA build pins the whole tree to x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-gcc-14
(sys-devel/gcc:14 is pulled in automatically). Set STRATA_CUDA_HOST_GCC in
package.env if your toolkit wants a different gcc slot.

Known issue: with Portage's pid-namespace sandbox, nvcc can hang in
do_wait with zombie children during the kernel compile. If the build
stalls at a high ninja step count for many minutes with zero CPU, add to
/etc/portage/env/strata-pid-ns.conf:

    PID_SANDBOX=disable

and reference it from package.env next to the lines above.

Without USE=cuda/hip Strata installs without an engine binary: upstream
builds the engine only for CUDA or HIP. In that setup let `strata setup`
obtain an engine, or rebuild the package with the flag. USE=vision without
cuda/hip ships the picture reader as /usr/lib/strata/vision/strata-vision;
copy it into an engine folder next to the engine binary to use it (the
reader is looked up next to the engine, not on PATH).

Server service (systemd)
------------------------
The package installs strata.service and creates the system user strata (via
acct-user/strata); it does not enable the service, because a web server
starting on every boot must be an explicit decision:

    systemctl enable --now strata

The unit runs `strata serve` as that user with hardening; the engine
component folder is registered into /var/lib/strata automatically on first
start (by /usr/lib/strata/engine-register, run as ExecStartPre).

* /etc/strata/daemon.conf      - STRATA_HOST / STRATA_PORT / STRATA_CONFIG
* /etc/strata/strata.json      - engine config template (root:strata 0640)

strata.json ships with REPLACE placeholders for the model path, tokenizer
and model name - the service fails at start until you point them at real
files, e.g. models under /var/lib/strata/models (own them with
`chown -R strata:strata /var/lib/strata/models`). After editing:

    systemctl restart strata

By default the API listens on 127.0.0.1 only. To expose it (STRATA_HOST=
0.0.0.0) the server refuses to start without an `"api_key"` entry added to
/etc/strata/strata.json - set one first. The shipped strata.json sets
`"log": "/var/lib/strata/strata.log"`, so the server and the engine append
their output to that file (rotated by hand or logrotate, Portage does not
touch it); the journal keeps the unit-level messages:

    journalctl -u strata

To keep everything in the journal instead, drop the `"log"` key from
strata.json and the engine inherits the server's stdout.

Configuration updates
---------------------
/etc/strata is under Portage's CONFIG_PROTECT: your edits to strata.json
and daemon.conf survive an upgrade. The new package version's files land
next to them as ._cfg0000_strata.json (and ._cfg0000_daemon.conf); merge
them with etc-update or dispatch-conf:

    etc-update

If you kept a heavily edited strata.json and only want one new upstream
key, copy that key across by hand instead of taking the new file whole.
The unit file itself is not protected - it lives under /usr and is
replaced on every merge; keep local overrides in
/etc/systemd/system/strata.service.d/ drop-ins (systemctl edit strata).

CUDA note (USE=cuda, sm_120 / RTX 50)
-------------------------------------
Upstream warns that engines built with CUDA < 13.0 can crash on long
prompts on sm_120 cards (engine issues #220, #224) and prints a CMake
warning when built with CUDA 12.x. Build against
dev-util/nvidia-cuda-toolkit >= 13 when available (the bentoo repo has
13.5) and rebuild this package afterwards; the installed engine ships
its own CUDA runtime libs, so upgrading the toolkit does not break the
running engine until you rebuild.

Minimum NVIDIA driver
---------------------
When registering the engine, package_engine.py records a minimum driver
version (default 570.124.06, the oldest R570 branch release that CUDA
12.8 toolkits require); strata refuses to start an engine whose driver
is older. If your driver branch is older but works, or you built against
a newer toolkit, override the threshold in /etc/portage/package.env
(STRATA_NVIDIA_DRIVER="570.86") and rebuild - a wrong threshold only
relaxes or tightens this self-check, it does not change what the engine
links against.

Monitor (USE=monitor)
---------------------
`strata monitor` is a textual-based TUI. The overlay vendors
dev-python/textual-8.2.8 (a pure-python package built from the GitHub
release), so no external repository is needed:

    emerge -av dev-python/textual

Models
------
No model weights ship with the package. Use `strata setup` or
`strata models` to download them into the per-user data directory.

Coexistence with other Strata installs
--------------------------------------
The CLI here shares the per-user data directory (~/.local/share/strata)
with desktop/standalone installs. A newer CLI migrates instance configs on
sight (e.g. the RAM budget rule), so if another Strata version owns that
directory, run package smokes against an isolated home first:

    HOME=$(mktemp -d) strata --help

HIP note
--------
The HIP branch has not yet been exercised on real ROCm hardware by this
overlay; report failures with the build log. STRATA_HIP_ARCHS overrides
the default "gfx1100;gfx1201".
